## 2. Market Clarity (NEW in v1.8)

### The Hard Truth

| Market | Test Type | Our Value | Moat Strength |
|--------|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| **QA Teams** | UI/E2E | Full framework, MCP tools, 9-step process | STRONG |
| **Developers** | Unit/Integration | Pre-packaged DDs, convenience | WEAK |

### Why QA Has Strong Moat

QA teams need UI/E2E testing:
- 4-layer architecture (Role → Task → Page → WebInterface)
- MCP tools automate complex workflows
- 9-step process handles page discovery, code generation
- Non-trivial to build from scratch (weeks/months)

### Why Developer Moat Is Weak

Developers doing unit/integration testing can DIY:
- Use AI + pytest directly
- Write their own standards/DDs
- No special framework needed
- We proved this during RAG development (73 tests, no framework needed)

### Strategic Decision

| Market | Strategy | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| **QA Teams** | Primary revenue target | Strong moat, willing to pay |
| **Developers** | Free tier / lead gen | Weak moat, use as funnel to QA product |

